<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa Cargo yr-on-yr yields down 3-4pc.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa Cargo yr-on-yr yields down 3-4pc.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yields for Lufthansa Cargo in October were three to four percent below the level of 12 months previously, Lufthansa said.</p>
<p>The cargo airline achieved its highest monthly tonnage growth of 1996 with a 7.2 percent rise, the latest Lufthansa monthly traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The following table shows traffic for October 1996.</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (1,000 tonnes)	157.1  up 7.2 pct</p>
<p>    Available cargo tonne-km (million) 827    down 0.1 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue cargo tonne-km (million)   608    up 6.7 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo load factor		  73.5   up 4.6 pct pts</p>
<p>    Americas (1,000 t)		 41.6   up 9.1 pct</p>
<p>    Asia-Pacific (1,000 t)	   39.9   up 9.6 pct</p>
<p>    Europe (1,000 t)		   71.6   up 4.8 pct</p>
<p>--Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
